※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4261
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4261 LANG_MASK_SHAPE_NOT_ONE_RUN

※ How wide a mask is depends on how many truth values there are, and the width
※ of a number is part of its type: a view whose type does not state its length
※ has no width to answer with.  Copied into an array that states it, it has.

fn first_bits(b: bool⟦⟧) → u8:
    ⎕mask(b)

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let b: bool⟦4⟧ = ⟦true, false, true, false⟧ in ⎕static
    if first_bits(b) = 5u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
